        "evidence": "enveloping-algebra.md:10-12 says monomials form a 'C-basis' of U(su(2)), but su(2) is a real Lie algebra (real form) generated by e1,e2,e3.",
        "notes": "A C-basis (md:11) presupposes the complex enveloping algebra; for the real form su(2) the PBW C-basis is really that of U(su(2)_C) = U(sl(2,C)). The block silently works over C without stating the complexification, and uses both U(su(2)) and the quantum group U_q(su(2)). Standard abuse, but the base field / real-vs-complex form is left implicit (compare the repo's own base-ring discipline). Minor."
